---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="The game collects no data: your game is saved on your iPhone, with no accounts, ads or analytics. This website counts visits without cookies." crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy policy' }]}>
  <div class="card">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">The game collects nothing about you. This website only counts visits, without cookies and without knowing who you are.</p>
    <h2>The game</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No data is collected.</strong> The game doesn't send anything about you, your iPhone or how you play to us or to anyone else.</li>
      <li><strong>No account.</strong> There's nothing to sign up for and nothing to sign in to.</li>
      <li><strong>No ads and no analytics.</strong> The game has no advertising and no tracking of any kind.</li>
      <li><strong>Your game stays on your iPhone.</strong> Saves are files on your device. Deleting the game deletes them.</li>
      <li><strong>It plays offline.</strong> The other adventurers you meet and chat with are part of the game, not real people, and what you type in the chat never leaves your iPhone.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It sets no cookies and has no ads.</li>
      <li>It counts visits with Vercel Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and doesn't follow you from site to site. It records which page was opened, the page that linked to it, and roughly what kind of device, browser and country the visit came from. Visitors are counted without being identified.</li>
      <li>If you switch between day and night, your browser remembers the choice on your own device.</li>
      <li>Like every website, the company that hosts it (Vercel) handles your request to show you the page, which involves your IP address.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Because the game collects no data from anyone, it collects none from children.</p>
    <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new one will be on this page. {site.supportEmail ? <>Questions? Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.</> : <>Questions? See the <a href="/support/">support page</a>.</>}</p>
    <p class="small">Last updated 18 November 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
